      "id": "claim_385563926fc74856b9c92ec0f2df260b",
      "statement": "MediaFormat::all() derives the accepted formats from an exhaustive match (so adding an enum variant fails to compile until it is listed) and wire_value() emits the serde wire spelling such as \"Blu-Ray\" rather than the Rust variant name; MovieMetadataDto::from_domain() composes the two to serve GET /api/v1/movie-metadata, guaranteeing the assistant is offered exactly the values ownedMedia/ripQuality accept.",
